          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition Records: Stations 86\u2013370\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThis report analyzes 18 equipment records spanning six asset classes (turbines, compressors, heat exchangers, scrubbers, reactors, valves, and pipelines) across 17 stations. The dataset shows a fleet in generally serviceable condition but with **four units warranting priority intervention** (scrubber 4920, valve 8094, pipeline 1499, and turbine 9273), **three units requiring enhanced monitoring** (scrubber 2555, valve 2302, and scrubber 4236), and a cluster of thermodynamic anomalies \u2014 most notably **low-temperature operation at high pressure** on scrubber 2555 and turbine 5367 \u2014 that suggest instrument faults, control loop problems, or off-design process conditions rather than mechanical degradation. Recommended actions are prioritized in Section 6.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope, Data Quality, and Method\n\n### 1.1 Dataset\n\n| # | Unit | Type | Station | P (kPa) | T (\u00b0C) | Flow (m\u00b3/h) | Vib (mm/s) | Eff (%) |\n|---|------|------|---------",
