          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition Monitoring Records\n\n## 1. Scope and Data Overview\n\nThis report analyzes 18 condition-monitoring records from a multi-station gas/plant network. Each record contains five process/health parameters: **pressure (kPa), temperature (\u00b0C), flow (m\u00b3/h), vibration (mm/s RMS), and efficiency (%)**. Equipment types include pipelines, scrubbers, a turbine, condenser, heat exchanger, separator, reactor, pumps, and a compressor.\n\nBecause no explicit alarm limits or design datasheets were provided, this analysis uses standard industry reference points (ISO 10816/20816 vibration severity zones, typical thermal efficiency bands, and hydraulic sanity checks) to flag anomalies, infer likely failure modes, and recommend actions. Where a record is ambiguous, I state the assumptions explicitly.\n\n### 1.1 Fleet Summary Statistics\n\n| Parameter | Min | Max | Approx. Median |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Pressure (kPa) | 94 | 860 | ~400 |\n| Temperature (\u00b0C) | \u221219 | 176 | ~90 |\n| Flow (m\u00b3/h) | 11 | 874 | ~490 |\n| Vibration (mm/s)",
