          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Equipment Records: Stations 24\u2013386\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThis report analyzes 18 equipment records spanning six asset classes (pumps, turbines, reactors, condensers, scrubbers, and heat exchangers) across 17 stations. The dataset shows several units operating with anomalous parameters that warrant immediate attention. Three units present **critical risk profiles**: reactor 8632 (station 24) with severe vibration and depressed efficiency, turbine 8771 (station 242) with simultaneous high vibration, high pressure, and sub-zero temperature, and pump 5581 (station 111) with extreme pressure and vibration despite nominal efficiency. A further six units show degraded efficiency below 80%, suggesting fouling, wear, or process drift. Recommended actions range from immediate shutdown inspection to 90-day monitoring intervals.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Methodology and Interpretive Framework\n\n### 1.1 Data Characteristics\n\nEach record contains five measurement channels:\n\n| Channel | Symbol | Relevance |\n|---|---|---|\n| Pressure | P (kPa) | Process duty point; deviations indicate blockage, leakage, or control faults |\n| Temperature | T (\u00b0C) | Thermal health; extremes suggest cooling",
