          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition-Monitoring Records (Records 0000000\u20130000017)\n\n## 1. Scope and Method\n\nThis report analyzes 18 condition-monitoring records spanning eight asset classes (scrubbers, heat exchangers, condensers, pipelines, valves, pumps, turbines, separators, and reactors) across stations ranging from 9 to 331. Each record contains five measured parameters: pressure (kPa), temperature (\u00b0C), flow (m\u00b3/h), vibration (mm/s RMS), and efficiency (%).\n\nBecause the dataset contains no explicit alarm limits, this analysis applies standard industry reference thresholds, principally ISO 10816/20816 vibration severity zones for rotating and reciprocating machinery, and typical thermal-performance expectations for heat-transfer and separation equipment. Where a parameter is anomalous relative to the asset class and the rest of the fleet, it is flagged, and the most probable failure modes are ranked. The report concludes with a prioritized maintenance action plan.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Fleet-Wide Screening\n\n### 2.1 Vibration Distribution\n\n| Vibration band | ISO 10816 zone (typical rigid mounting, Class II\u2013III machines) | Records |\n|---|---|---|\n| \u2264",
